# The build context is the repository, and everything in here is either not
# needed to build the binary or not something an image should ever contain.
#
# The two that matter most are at the end: a `.git` directory in a build context is
# every commit this repository has ever made, and the Dockerfile stages the whole
# context into the builder. `.dockerignore` is the only thing standing between a
# `docker build` and publishing the project's history into an image layer.

.git
.github
bin
dist
coverage.out
coverage-handwritten.out
data

# The data directory a local `make run` leaves behind. It is a DM's campaign, and it
# has no business being in an image layer.
vault

# Docs and tests are not needed to build the binary, and the tests would pull the
# whole module graph into the context.
docs
e2e
**/*_test.go
**/testdata
